course: dictionary
lesson: 10684
title: Unpredictable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «unpredictable» is built from three parts: un- means not, predict means to say what will happen before it happens, and -able means can be. So unpredictable means cannot be known beforehand.
explain: Context gives you a clue. «Hyperion is a lumpy moon like a sponge, full of deep craters, and it tumbles chaotically, in a messy, unpredictable way, as it orbits.» The words after the comma explain chaotically, so you can guess that a messy, unpredictable way means a movement you cannot guess.
explain: You can use the word in your own life. A dice roll is unpredictable, but if you roll many times you can spot patterns. An unknown dog can be unpredictable, so always ask before you stroke it.
fact: Unpredictable means impossible to know or say beforehand what will happen.
fact: An unpredictable person or animal behaves in ways you cannot guess, sometimes calm and sometimes not.
fact: The prefix un- often means not, as in unhappy, unkind and unpredictable.
fact: Weather, earthquakes and volcanoes can be unpredictable, although scientists study patterns to make better guesses.
fact: «Hyperion ... tumbles chaotically, in a messy, unpredictable way, as it orbits» shows that unpredictable can describe how something moves.
exercise: What does unpredictable mean? | Easy to guess | *Impossible to know beforehand what will happen | Very loud and noisy | Always the same every time
exercise: Which of these is unpredictable? | The sun rising in the east each morning | A clock striking twelve at noon | *A single dice roll | Two plus two makes four
exercise: In «Hyperion ... tumbles chaotically, in a messy, unpredictable way, as it orbits», which phrase explains chaotically? | *in a messy, unpredictable way | as it orbits | deep craters | lumpy moon
test: Why should you ask before stroking an unknown dog? | Because stroking makes dogs shrink | *Because an unknown dog can be unpredictable | Because dogs cannot feel touch | Because dogs only eat in the morning
test: Maisie says unpredictable means easy to guess. Is she right? | Yes, it means always the same | Yes, it means easy to guess | *No, unpredictable means impossible to know beforehand | No, it means very fast
exam: Which best describes an unpredictable character in a story? | *One who keeps readers guessing | One who never changes at all | One who is always asleep | One who is always the same
